      "note": [
        "Statistics Sweden has departed from the principle that research and development (R & D) should be considered as support activities from November 2016. This means that more companies are found in industry 72 according to the Swedish Standard Industrial Classification 2007. This affects the survey as of the 2nd quarter 2017. ",
        "In accordance with international guidelines, a number of joint stock companies have been reclassified with regard to sector, from the business sector to public administration. This affects the statistics published from the second quarter of 2019 and forward.",
        "As of the second quarter 2021, short-term employment statistics use new auxiliary information, which is applied in the design and estimation stages of production. A yearly mean value has replaced information on the number of persons employed at an enterprise at a single point in time. This has resulted in an increase in the number of employees in, for example, tenant owners associations (under section L, property management). This change has not been considered large enough to warrant a break in the time series."
      ],
